From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 11:58:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] __memory: guard empty range relocate to avoid null memcpy
 UBSan

The trivially relocatable fast path in __uninitialized_allocator_relocate
calls __builtin_memcpy unconditionally. When the source range is empty
(for example growing an empty vector) the pointers can be null, and
passing null to memcpy violates its nonnull argument attribute, which
-fsanitize=undefined reports at runtime even though the copy size is
zero. llvm17 used an element by element move loop that naturally did
nothing for an empty range, so this only regressed after the llvm21
upgrade. Skip the memcpy when the range is empty to match that behavior.

Signed-off-by: v-zhangxiaomeng5 <v-zhangxiaomeng5@xiaomi.com>
---
 include/__memory/uninitialized_algorithms.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/__memory/uninitialized_algorithms.h b/include/__memory/uninitialized_algorithms.h
index e802366400..1347cbedbd 100644
--- a/include/__memory/uninitialized_algorithms.h
+++ b/include/__memory/uninitialized_algorithms.h
@@ -633,7 +633,7 @@ _LIBCPP_HIDE_FROM_ABI _LIBCPP_CONSTEXPR_SINCE_CXX14 void __uninitialized_allocat
     }
     __guard.__complete();
     std::__allocator_destroy(__alloc, __first, __last);
-  } else {
+  } else if (__first != __last) {
     // Casting to void* to suppress clang complaining that this is technically UB.
     __builtin_memcpy(static_cast<void*>(std::__to_address(__result)),
                      std::__to_address(__first),
